os","text":"To solve this problem, we need to understand the geometric configuration and the probability calculation involved.\n\n1. **Identify the Geometry and Setup**:\n    - Rectangle \\(ABCD\\) has center \\(O\\).\n    - The ratio \\(\\frac{AB}{AD} = k\\).\n    - We need to find the probability that a randomly chosen point inside the rectangle is closer to \\(O\\) than to any of the four vertices.\n\n2. **Determine the Regions**:\n    - The region closer to \\(O\\) than to any vertex will be bounded by perpendicular bisectors of segments joining \\(O\\) to each vertex.\n    - Each bisector will divide the rectangle into two regions, and the intersection of these regions will form a smaller rectangle centered at \\(O\\).\n\n3. **Equations of Perpendicular Bisectors**:\n    - Consider the rectangle with \\(A = (-a, b)\\), \\(B = (a, b)\\), \\(C = (a, -b)\\), and \\(D = (-a, -b)\\).\n    - The center \\(O = (0, 0)\\).\n    - The perpendicular bisector of \\(OA\\) (which is the line segment joining \\(O\\) to \\(A\\)) will be the line \\(x = \\frac{a}{2}\\).\n    - Similarly, the perpendicular bisectors of \\(OB\\), \\(OC\\), and \\(OD\\) will be \\(x = -\\frac{a}{2}\\), \\(y = \\frac{b}{2}\\), and \\(y = -\\frac{b}{2}\\) respectively.\n\n4. **Smaller Rectangle Formed**:\n    - The region closer to \\(O\\) than to any vertex is a smaller rectangle with sides parallel to the original rectangle and centered at \\(O\\).\n    - The side lengths of this smaller rectangle are \\(\\frac{a}{2}\\) and \\(\\frac{b}{2}\\).\n\n5. **Area Calculation**:\n    - The area of the original rectangle is \\(2a \\cdot 2b = 4ab\\).\n    - The area of the smaller rectangle is \\(\\frac{a}{2} \\cdot \\frac{b}{2} = \\frac{ab}{4}\\).\n\n6. **Probability Calculation**:\n    - The probability that a randomly chosen point is closer to \\(O\\) than to any vertex is the ratio of the area of the smaller rectangle to the area of the original rectangle.\n    - Therefore, the probability is \\(\\frac{\\frac{ab}{4}}{4ab} = \\frac{1}{16}\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{1}{4}}\n\\]\n\nThe correct probability should be \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{4}}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{1}{4}}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
